<h2 id="sec-1">A comparison decided by the calendar</h2>
<p>Most head-to-head rental comparisons in Hanoi are settled at the daily rate, where even a small gap compounds over a stay. The Honda Vision and Honda Air Blade refuse that shortcut. Their verified rates agree exactly at 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week, so for anything shorter than a month the price question answers itself: there is no difference to find. The comparison only becomes interesting at the monthly tier, where the two rate cards finally part ways.</p>
<p>The parting is not the one most renters expect. The Air Blade carries a flat monthly rate of 1,500,000 VND, while the Vision is published as a range of 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month. That puts the sportier-looking machine below the comfort-focused one by 300,000 to 500,000 VND over a month, a direction that surprises anyone who assumes price follows engine character rather than the shop’s published card.</p>
<p>This guide works through the two rate cards with verified figures only: no invented discounts, no speculated promotions, no invented availability. The method is simple. Read where the cards agree, read where they diverge, then match the divergence to the length of your stay. Below a month the cards are identical; at a month the calendar decides for you.</p>
<h2 id="sec-2">The verified rates side by side</h2>
<p>The Vision’s card reads 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month, with the monthly figure published as a range whose final tier is confirmed at the counter. It is the step-up automatic of the fleet, priced one full tier above the 150,000 VND entry class that the Honda Click, Yamaha Mio, Honda Wave and Yamaha Sirius occupy.</p>
<p>The Air Blade’s card reads 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and 1,500,000 VND per month, the monthly figure quoted flat. Day for day and week for week the two machines are indistinguishable on price, which makes this the only pairing in the fleet where a real cost difference hides entirely inside a single row of the rate card.</p>
<p>The size of that hidden difference is between 300,000 VND, measured against the floor of the Vision’s range, and 500,000 VND against its ceiling. For orientation, that is roughly two to three days of the entry tier’s 150,000 VND daily rate, a gap worth understanding before a long stay rather than after it. The full fleet structure behind both cards is charted in the guide to <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a>.</p>
<h2 id="sec-3">Where the two machines agree</h2>
<p>Both machines sit on the same rung of the fleet’s price ladder. The entry tier rents at 150,000 VND per day and 700,000 VND per week; the Vision and Air Blade both represent the step above it at 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week. A renter who has already decided to pay the step-up rate is choosing between two members of the same tier, not between a cheap and an expensive option.</p>
<p>The weekly arithmetic is identical too. On either card, seven days cost 1,000,000 VND, which is exactly five times the 200,000 VND daily rate, so neither machine offers a weekly bargain the other lacks. Renters who stack short weeks pay the same money whichever machine they ride, and any plan built around weekly renewals is cost-neutral between the two.</p>
<p>Agreement this complete changes what the decision is about. For a weekend, a week or a fortnight, price cannot break the tie because price never differs, so the choice becomes which machine you would rather ride and how it fits you, questions of comfort and preference rather than arithmetic. Those are worth asking at the counter, and cost should stay out of them until the stay reaches a month.</p>
<h2 id="sec-4">Where the pricing diverges</h2>
<p>The divergence at the monthly tier is structural as well as numerical. The Vision’s month is published as a range, which means the final tier for a given rental is confirmed with the shop before it is booked, while the Air Blade’s month is a flat figure that reads the same for every monthly renter. One card flexes within a published band; the other does not flex at all.</p>
<p>Inside that structure sits the arithmetic. A month on the Air Blade costs 1,500,000 VND. A month on the Vision costs 1,800,000 VND at the bottom of its range and 2,000,000 VND at the top, so the premium for choosing the Vision over the Air Blade is 300,000 to 500,000 VND depending on where the confirmed tier lands. On any shorter period that premium is zero.</p>
<p>Nothing else on either card diverges, and nothing on either card invents extras. There is no verified promotion that bundles the gap away and no published discount that closes it; if anyone quotes you a price below these published figures, treat it as something to confirm with the shop directly rather than a fact to plan around. Verified numbers, confirmed at the counter, are the whole basis of this comparison.</p>
<h2 id="sec-5">Short stays: when money is off the table</h2>
<p>For short stays, money is off the table by design. A few days on either machine cost 200,000 VND each, a week costs 1,000,000 VND on either card, and no period under a month produces a different bill. A renter who chooses between the Vision and the Air Blade on price for a short visit is choosing between two identical numbers, which is to say not choosing anything.</p>
<p>What remains is the part of the decision price cannot answer: fit. How the riding position suits you, how the machine feels on the routes you plan to ride, whether you prefer the character of one over the other, and practical questions about carrying a passenger or luggage that depend on your trip. None of these carry a price tag on either card, and all of them are legitimate tie-breakers.</p>
<p>The practical move for a short stay is to ask to see both machines. Because the short-stay pricing is identical, comparing them in person costs you nothing, and the shop can tell you on the spot which is available and how each fits your plan. Choosing by comfort under a month is free; the only expensive version of this choice is the monthly one.</p>
<h2 id="sec-6">Monthly rentals: the real decision</h2>
<p>At the monthly tier the comparison earns its keep. A month on the Air Blade is a flat 1,500,000 VND. A month on the Vision is 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND with the tier confirmed at the counter, so the monthly renter is choosing between a flat figure and a range that starts above it. This is the only period where the two cards produce different bills.</p>
<p>Set the monthly rates against the alternative of stacking weeks. Four consecutive weeks cost 4,000,000 VND on either card, since both carry the same 1,000,000 VND weekly rate. Against that baseline, the monthly tier saves 2,000,000 to 2,200,000 VND on the Vision and 2,500,000 VND on the Air Blade, so the monthly rate is the correct instrument on both cards, and it rewards the Air Blade renter more.</p>
<p>The counter-intuitive result is worth stating plainly: the machine with the sportier reputation is the cheaper month. A renter who prefers the Vision and stays a month pays a premium of 300,000 to 500,000 VND for that preference, not for any published bundle of extras, because none exists on either card. Preference is a fine reason to pay it; an imagined saving is not, and the shop’s verified numbers are the honest basis for either choice.</p>
<h2 id="sec-7">Choosing by length of stay</h2>
<p>A few days: either machine, same money, 200,000 VND per day. Choose by fit, availability and how the machine matches the riding you have planned, and let price stay out of it entirely because price has nothing to say. The same holds for a single week, which bills identically at 1,000,000 VND on both cards.</p>
<p>One to three weeks: the week rate covers seven days identically on both cards and the daily rate fills the edges, so mixed stays still cost the same on either machine. The tie remains unbroken by money, and the decision stays where it belongs, in comfort and preference. As the stay stretches toward four weeks, the monthly tier starts to matter and the question changes character.</p>
<p>A month or longer: this is the Air Blade’s territory on price, at 1,500,000 VND flat against the Vision’s 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND range. The longer the stay, the more the 300,000 to 500,000 VND gap matters, and for stays beyond a single month only the monthly tier is published, so confirm the best arrangement for your dates with the shop directly. A longer overview of multi-week planning sits in the main <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> resource.</p>
<h2 id="sec-8">Questions to settle at the counter</h2>
<p>For the Vision, the question to settle is where inside the published 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND monthly range your rental lands. The range is verified, but its final tier is confirmed per rental, so ask for the exact monthly figure before you commit, and treat the answer as the number your budget is built on rather than either end of the range.</p>
<p>For either machine, confirm availability for your dates and the practicalities of the rental itself: what documents and deposit the shop expects, and what applies to your licence situation, which depends on the licence you hold and where it was issued rather than on the machine you pick. The general answers to these logistics questions are collected in the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>, and the counter is the place to confirm your specific case.</p>
<p>The counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00. Because short-stay pricing is identical between the two machines, you lose nothing by asking to compare both in person, and because monthly pricing is not, you gain the most by settling the Vision’s tier in the same conversation. One visit answers every open question on both cards.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions about Honda Vision vs Honda Air Blade rental costs in Hanoi</h2>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>How much does it cost to rent a Honda Vision in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>Verified prices at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu put the Honda Vision at 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month, with the final monthly tier confirmed at the counter. The shop is at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi and is open daily from 09:00 to 21:00.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>How much does it cost to rent a Honda Air Blade in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>Verified prices put the Honda Air Blade at 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and a flat 1,500,000 VND per month. Day and week rates are identical to the Honda Vision, so the two cards differ only at the monthly tier, where the Air Blade is the cheaper of the pair.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Which is cheaper, the Honda Vision or the Honda Air Blade?</h2>
<p>For daily and weekly rentals they cost exactly the same, 200,000 VND per day and 1,000,000 VND per week on both cards. At the monthly tier the Air Blade is cheaper by 300,000 to 500,000 VND, at 1,500,000 VND flat against the Vision’s published 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND range.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Is a monthly rental cheaper than paying week by week?</h2>
<p>Yes, on both cards. Four consecutive weeks cost 4,000,000 VND at the shared weekly rate of 1,000,000 VND, while a month costs 1,500,000 VND on the Air Blade and 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND on the Vision. The monthly tier saves money on either machine and saves more on the Air Blade.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Which machine should I choose for a short stay in Hanoi?</h2>
<p>For anything shorter than a month the cost is identical, so choose by fit and preference rather than price. Ask to see both machines at the shop, compare how each suits your routes and plans, and check availability for your dates. Price gives you no help below the monthly tier, and it is not supposed to.</p>
</article>
<article class="faq-entry">
<h2>Where can I confirm the exact monthly price before renting?</h2>
<p>At the counter of Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00. The Vision’s monthly range of 1,800,000 to 2,000,000 VND is confirmed per rental, and the Air Blade’s 1,000,000 VND weekly and 1,500,000 VND monthly figures can be checked against your dates in the same visit.</p>
</article>
